From 0d56099f4609a6596b74241cfa4820a8c92cc85e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:40:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: take the display's new modes while Kodi runs

Kodi read the modes of the display once, when it started, and a resolution
names its mode by its place in the list of the connector (its strId). A TV
input whose setting changes the EDID (HDMI Deep Colour, a game mode), or
another display on the same output, kept the modes of the start until Kodi
started again: a mode that the display no longer takes stayed on the screen,
one that it offers since was not offered, and the HDMI 1.4 notice has to say
"restart".

Kodi's other window systems make their resolutions again while it runs: X11
(NotifyXRREvent(): UpdateResolutions(), then RecreateWindow() finds the mode
on the screen in the new list by its id, or takes the desktop resolution),
Android (UpdateDisplayModes(): UpdateResolutions(false) keeps the desktop
resolution, found by its size, refresh rate and flags), Wayland and Windows.
GBM does the same now. ModeListRefresh.h decides; RefreshModes() does it:

- only after a hot-plug event of the device in use, 3 s after the last one and
  10 s after a video (as the display watch waits), and only while nothing is in
  the way: nothing plays; the output shows the interface alone (what a move to
  another output waits for: no video plane, no HDR or HDR10+ signalling, no
  change of mode held for a video, nothing of native Dolby Vision); no modeset
  and no reset of the display pending; no dialog (the question to keep a
  resolution among them); no screen calibration, no slideshow, no interface in
  3D; the display of Kodi awake. Without such an event nothing at all is done:
  each frame compares two counts;
- the display is probed then, as a video that starts after such an event
  probes it (CDisplayLook). Not connected, no EDID that can be read, or the EDID
  the resolutions were made with: nothing is done (debug lines only). Another
  EDID with the same modes in the same places: nothing either;
- other modes: the mode on the screen, the desktop resolution's and the current
  resolution's are found in the new list by their timing (SameTiming() of
  CCommittedMode), never by their place, and the resolutions are made again of
  the new list (MakeResolutions(): UpdateResolutions() with the desktop
  resolution given). A resolution whose mode is no longer offered becomes what
  a start takes for it: the desktop resolution the mode the display prefers
  (FindPreferredMode()), the current one that of the settings or the nearest
  (GetDisplayResolution()). Where the mode on the screen is still offered,
  nothing changes on the screen: its resolution takes its new place
  (ApplyModeChange(), as for a mode that the system set). Where it is not, the
  interface is set in the current resolution (SetVideoResolution(), forced, as
  X11's RecreateWindow() and SetResolutionAfterMove() set it);
- fail-closed: a list that cannot be matched (no mode, two modes with one
  timing, no mode without a 3D layout, the mode on the screen in 3D) changes
  nothing, and the user is told that a restart takes the new modes; so is a
  resolution set for them that the driver refuses. What was read of the
  connector before is kept, as CDRMConnector::Refresh() keeps it.

In kodi.log without debug: "Modes: the display of <output> has other modes
(N -> M): the resolutions are made again of them. ..." with what the interface,
the desktop and the current resolution became; "Modes: ... another EDID, with
the N modes that the resolutions were made of: nothing is done"; and the
warnings of a refusal. Notifications #39955, #39956 and #39957, translated in
Estuary (#31975-#31977, es_ES, es_AR, es_MX).

Host test of the header (outside the tree): its parts; a TV that leaves and
enters HDMI 1.4 mode, a monitor instead of the TV and back, the same modes
with other types, duplicates, no modes, 3D modes only; and 20000 random lists.
The same checks fail with the behaviour of before (the list of the start kept:
23 checks of the cases, 17113 of the random lists) and with a refresh that
keeps the numbers of the resolutions (19 and 16246). 19 mutations of the
header caught. Nothing of this has run on a graphics card.
